  "goodToKnow": "Die Synagoge is a synagogue. On 9 November 1938, during the Novemberpogrome (sometimes called Reichskristallnacht), the Nazis burned and destroyed some 1,400 synagogues and prayer rooms across Germany and Austria. Today, Jewish life in Germany has grown again, partly through immigration from the former Soviet Union, and new synagogues have opened in cities such as Munich and Dresden. Synagogues are often protected by police. Plural: die Synagogen."
